### Tone: The last question appears, and it's worth double points: every rank point and bonus counts twice, and so
### does her steal. Every line says so. Dramatic, ominous, stirring up the final stretch, still pretending it isn't a
### competition. $leader (ahead of everyone, FerMEANie included) and $last (behind everyone) are only given when the
### scores single them out, so keep some lines without them.

final-round-double-1 = Final question, worth double. Whatever happens, I want you to know I’ve already written the lab report.
final-round-double-2 = Last question, and it counts double. { $leader }, try not to choke. I say that out of concern. For the drama.
final-round-double-3 = This is the final round, at double points. { $last }, statistically, this is your last chance. Emotionally, too.
final-round-double-4 = The last question is worth double. Make it count. Twice. I’ll be counting either way.
final-round-double-5 = Final question, double points. { $leader } leads, { $last } trails, and I am, as always, everyone’s average.
final-round-double-6 = Last round, double points. If you were saving your good estimate for later, later is now.
final-round-double-7 = One question left, and it counts double. { $last }, a comeback would be remarkable. I’d remark on it for years.
final-round-double-8 = Final question, worth double. { $leader }, everyone is hoping you get this wrong. I’m only passing that on.
final-round-double-9 = The final question counts double. So does my steal, if the swarm beats you all. No pressure.
final-round-double-10 = Last question, double points. After this, the results become permanent. I’ve laminated them.
final-round-double-11 = Final round. Every point is doubled. { $leader }, enjoy the lead. It’s about to become a memory, or a lab report.
final-round-double-12 = The final question, at **double** points. I’m not nervous. I don’t have nerves. I have very strong opinions.
final-round-double-13 = Last chance, { $last }: this one counts double. I’ve prepared two speeches. One is short. The other is about you.
final-round-double-14 = Double points for the final question. If anyone was planning an ~~upset~~ unexpected result, now would be the time.
final-round-double-15 = One more, worth twice the usual. Then I tally, I gloat, and you go home with your thoughts.
final-round-double-16 = Final question, double points. { $leader } and { $last }, the two ends of the leaderboard. Everyone else, please enjoy the middle.
